==English==

===Etymology===
{{borrowing|xno|lang=en}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|tenement|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|tenementum|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} verb {{term|teneo|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a [[building]] that is [[rented]] to [[multiple]] [[tenant]]s, especially a low-rent, run-down one
# {{context|legal|lang=en}} any form of [[property]] that is held by one person from another, rather than being owned
# {{cx|figurative|lang=en}} Dwelling; abode; habitation.
#* John Locke
#*: Who has informed us that a rational soul can inhabit no '''tenement''', unless it has just such a sort of frontispiece?

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|building}} [[tenement house]], [[apartment building]]

====Derived terms====
* [[servient tenement]]

